    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`HouseholdNormalizer.java`** \u2014 The household identifier is now deterministic from `(lastName, postcode)`:\n- `householdId(lastName, postcode)` now hashes `normalize(lastName) + \"|\" + postcode` and keeps the first **12** hex chars (was 32 hex chars over `lastName + \"\\n\" + address`).\n- Removed the now-unused `sameHousehold(...)` address-based matcher.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Reworked the duplicate/household logic in `addOwner`:\n- `householdId` is computed from `lastName` + `postcode` (was `lastName` + `address`), so owners with the same last name and postcode automatically share it.\n- `sharesHousehold` now **only bypasses the duplicate block** rather than creating the link. When it's not set, the new `rejectHouseholdDuplicate(householdId)` rejects any create whose `householdId` already exists (409). When it *is* set, the household check is skipped **and** the owner is not flagged as a possible duplicate (`possibleDuplicateOf` forced to `null`) \u2014 a declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\n- `buildIdentityKey` no longer takes `sharesHousehold`; the household segment always carries the deterministic `householdId`.\n- `householdSize` continues to key off the computed `householdId`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, and `identityKey` descriptions to document the deterministic `(lastName, postcode)` derivation and the new household-duplicate / declared-member behaviour.\n\n## Verification\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nThe acceptance test confirms the observable contract: same `lastName` + `postcode` yields the same `householdId` (with the second owner created via `sharesHousehold` to bypass the 409 block), and a different `lastName` yields a different `householdId`.\n\nOne thing worth noting: the existing 409 for a household duplicate reuses `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (it already maps to 409 Conflict), so its `errors` property still reports `\"identityKey\"`. If you'd prefer a distinct `\"household\"`/`\"sharesHousehold\"` error label on that response, I can add a dedicated exception \u2014 no current test asserts on it.",
